# LIFESYNC OS License

### Recommended project license
Use a permissive open-source license appropriate for the project owner’s intended redistribution model. The exact license MUST be selected and placed here before public release.

### Third-party license rule
Third-party components MUST retain their required notices and attribution. The project MUST NOT claim ownership of third-party source code.

### Dependency provenance
Every copied, forked, vendored, patched, or embedded third-party component MUST be recorded in `docs/third-party/licenses.md` with:
- project name;
- repository URL;
- exact version or commit;
- license;
- whether source was modified;
- where integrated;
- redistribution obligations;
- attribution obligations.

